WEBVTT

00:00:00.740 --> 00:00:02.570
Rabbit!

00:00:02.570 --> 00:00:06.020
Rabbit meat!

00:00:06.020 --> 00:00:09.790
I hope we can catch one soon!

00:00:06.310 --> 00:00:10.230
<b>A Strange Turban Shell</b>

00:00:10.820 --> 00:00:13.240
It would be nice if it
gets caught in the trap.

00:00:14.340 --> 00:00:16.870
Shion-san! Welcome back!

00:00:17.770 --> 00:00:20.200
Y-You brought back quite a bit...

00:00:20.720 --> 00:00:22.910
It was pretty difficult
as I was all by myself.

00:00:23.430 --> 00:00:24.950
So...

00:00:24.950 --> 00:00:26.710
Did you get what you were after?

00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:30.070
No. You can't catch things that quickly.

00:00:30.070 --> 00:00:33.090
If we're lucky, we might get
something in two or three days.

00:00:34.830 --> 00:00:36.310
Then today...

00:00:37.140 --> 00:00:39.350
What are we going to do
about dinner tonight?

00:00:39.350 --> 00:00:41.930
This is no time to be sitting
around pleased with yourselves!

00:00:43.160 --> 00:00:45.350
<i>Now you mention it, that's true.</i>

00:00:45.780 --> 00:00:49.230
D-Don't worry. I'll go find something.

00:00:50.200 --> 00:00:52.810
It's just going to be rock shells
or hermit crabs or something, right?

00:00:52.810 --> 00:00:55.360
Day after day, it's always the same thing...

00:00:55.360 --> 00:00:57.770
I-I'll find something different today...

00:00:57.770 --> 00:01:00.920
Oh, that's right. If I go diving,
I might be able to find turban shells.

00:01:00.920 --> 00:01:02.250
I've been thinking about it for a while.

00:01:02.250 --> 00:01:03.710
Really?

00:01:03.710 --> 00:01:06.210
I like turban shells. They're good
grilled in their own shells.

00:01:06.770 --> 00:01:08.420
Do your best to go get some, okay?

00:01:08.420 --> 00:01:10.000
Good luck!

00:01:10.940 --> 00:01:14.390
That's the first time I've
ever seen you flustered.

00:01:25.390 --> 00:01:25.680
<b>Are You Lost?</b>

00:01:25.680 --> 00:01:28.480
<b>Are You Lost?</b>

00:02:18.750 --> 00:02:19.700
Here?

00:02:19.700 --> 00:02:20.610
Yes.

00:02:21.210 --> 00:02:24.270
The water's deeper here than
the place I usually go to find things.

00:02:25.620 --> 00:02:27.910
It's probably about 10 meters deep.

00:02:28.450 --> 00:02:31.720
You can't get large shellfish like
turban shells without diving.

00:02:31.720 --> 00:02:32.840
Really?

00:02:33.250 --> 00:02:34.500
Right. Let's go.

00:02:35.070 --> 00:02:35.930
Yeah!

00:02:45.530 --> 00:02:46.830
<i>Whoa!</i>

00:02:46.830 --> 00:02:48.500
<i>It's so dark! And scary!</i>

00:02:48.500 --> 00:02:50.560
<i>I can't see anything that way...</i>

00:02:51.820 --> 00:02:53.170
<i>Where's Homare?</i>

00:02:55.250 --> 00:02:58.570
<i>Is Homare gonna be okay diving that deep?</i>

00:02:59.290 --> 00:03:02.780
<i>Humans can only make
out vague shapes underwater.</i>

00:03:02.780 --> 00:03:08.540
<i>But you can use the air in your lungs
to improvise underwater glasses.</i>

00:03:09.410 --> 00:03:12.930
<i>There seem to be the same kinds
of fish you'd find off Japan's coasts.</i>

00:03:13.540 --> 00:03:16.440
<i>If we can catch fish,
we aren't likely to starve.</i>

00:03:16.970 --> 00:03:20.050
<i>But, I don't see any turban shells...</i>

00:03:20.450 --> 00:03:22.340
<i>I'll give up on those
and get the usual shellfish.</i>

00:03:22.840 --> 00:03:25.430
It's just going to be rock shells
or hermit crabs or something, right?

00:03:30.350 --> 00:03:32.110
<i>I suppose I could hold out a little longer.</i>

00:03:35.230 --> 00:03:36.840
We're back!

00:03:37.270 --> 00:03:39.090
Welcome back!

00:03:39.090 --> 00:03:41.790
Look! Look! We found this!

00:03:41.790 --> 00:03:43.800
We thought it might make a good pot.

00:03:43.800 --> 00:03:44.410
Huh?

00:03:45.940 --> 00:03:47.200
Oh!

00:03:47.620 --> 00:03:49.620
That's amazing! You found that much?

00:03:49.620 --> 00:03:51.750
Just what we'd expect from you, Homare-san!

00:03:54.090 --> 00:03:55.790
Oh dear, you dropped—

00:03:58.170 --> 00:04:01.450
Th-Those are very
strange-looking turban shells...

00:04:01.450 --> 00:04:02.880
They look like stars...

00:04:02.880 --> 00:04:04.310
Where are you going, Shion?

00:04:04.310 --> 00:04:06.100
The ocean's that way!

00:04:06.880 --> 00:04:10.580
This is a Northern Pacific sea star,
one of the few edible starfish,

00:04:10.580 --> 00:04:12.180
and it needs to be boiled.

00:04:12.180 --> 00:04:14.270
There's foam forming.

00:04:14.690 --> 00:04:17.240
That's due to water-soluble saponins.

00:04:17.240 --> 00:04:18.520
They can have a sterilizing effect.

00:04:18.880 --> 00:04:20.910
It will help disinfect the pot, too.

00:04:20.910 --> 00:04:24.450
I see. That's very reassuring, 
isn't it, Shion-san?

00:04:25.370 --> 00:04:27.440
Don't worry, Shion-san!

00:04:27.440 --> 00:04:30.460
I've heard there's a region of
Kyushu where they eat starfish!

00:04:30.460 --> 00:04:33.050
It's just a new kind of turban shell...

00:04:33.050 --> 00:04:34.470
No good. She's done.

00:04:35.350 --> 00:04:37.040
They should be just about ready.

00:04:37.820 --> 00:04:39.290
If you turn them upside
down and break them open,

00:04:39.290 --> 00:04:41.790
you'll find egg sacs, similar to sea urchins.

00:04:42.200 --> 00:04:43.720
This is the part you can eat.

00:04:44.370 --> 00:04:46.840
Here, Shion. It tastes
a lot like sea urchin, too.

00:04:50.260 --> 00:04:51.410
Your hand?

00:04:52.530 --> 00:04:54.020
She hurt herself.

00:04:54.350 --> 00:04:56.830
She found oysters and tried
to harvest some, but...

00:04:56.830 --> 00:04:59.780
the shells are really sharp, like razors.

00:05:00.230 --> 00:05:02.680
She was trying to pry them
up with her bare hands...

00:05:04.340 --> 00:05:05.830
They're nice and hot!

00:05:05.830 --> 00:05:07.240
There are lots more.

00:05:07.590 --> 00:05:10.610
You really managed to gather a lot!

00:05:10.610 --> 00:05:11.410
Yes.

00:05:13.340 --> 00:05:14.510
It's delicious...

00:05:15.860 --> 00:05:17.460
This starfish is delicious.

00:05:19.810 --> 00:05:21.840
It's even better than a turban shell!

00:05:23.780 --> 00:05:25.640
Really? I'm glad.

00:05:26.250 --> 00:05:28.090
Thank you, Homare-san.

00:05:28.930 --> 00:05:29.730
Sure.

00:05:30.300 --> 00:05:33.310
<b>Are You Lost?</b>

00:05:30.300 --> 00:05:33.310
The next
day, even
more starfish 
adorned 
the dinner 
table.

00:05:31.410 --> 00:05:33.310
Really?

00:05:37.220 --> 00:05:39.070
Mutsu. Are you all right?

00:05:39.070 --> 00:05:42.580
Hey! Hurry up you two!

00:05:42.580 --> 00:05:44.150
You're gonna get left behind!

00:05:44.480 --> 00:05:47.380
A-Asuka-san really has a lot of energy.

00:05:47.380 --> 00:05:50.030
Asuka! I told you to keep your voice down!

00:05:50.030 --> 00:05:51.240
The rabbits will run away!

00:05:51.240 --> 00:05:53.410
I know!

00:05:53.410 --> 00:05:56.030
I'll find the rabbit first and—

00:05:56.670 --> 00:05:58.500
Do rabbits...

00:05:58.500 --> 00:06:01.900
When they get caught in 
the trap... do they die?

00:06:01.900 --> 00:06:02.880
It depends.

00:06:03.350 --> 00:06:05.710
If they're alive, you have to finish them off.

00:06:05.710 --> 00:06:08.510
You stretch their necks out and
snap the cervical vertebrae.

00:06:08.510 --> 00:06:09.920
Can you do it?

00:06:09.920 --> 00:06:12.180
J-Just leave it to me!

00:06:12.570 --> 00:06:15.060
The trap was over there, wasn't it?

00:06:15.510 --> 00:06:17.570
<i>If it's alive, finish it off.</i>

00:06:17.570 --> 00:06:22.730
<i>I know what I said, but if there is
a rabbit I'll be both happy and sad...</i>

00:06:22.970 --> 00:06:23.650
There!

00:06:23.650 --> 00:06:24.620
Whoa!

00:06:24.620 --> 00:06:27.490
No way! I can't! There's no way I can do it!

00:06:27.490 --> 00:06:28.330
Huh?

00:06:28.330 --> 00:06:30.690
Oh. I got caught on a thorn. That's all.

00:06:33.930 --> 00:06:34.910
This is the place.

00:06:37.380 --> 00:06:38.890
Nothing's sprung the trap yet.

00:06:40.190 --> 00:06:42.960
I suppose they won't be caught that easily.

00:06:43.340 --> 00:06:46.880
When you're facing things in nature,
things don't always go the way you—

00:06:47.990 --> 00:06:48.800
Am I...

00:06:48.800 --> 00:06:49.800
...seeing things?

00:06:50.030 --> 00:06:50.960
Let's head back!

00:06:52.090 --> 00:06:53.660
Do you think it's a rescue team?

00:06:53.660 --> 00:06:55.310
I hope so.

00:06:57.710 --> 00:06:58.760
Shion!

00:06:59.260 --> 00:07:00.980
Do you see something?

00:07:03.460 --> 00:07:05.900
I... I don't know...

00:07:07.430 --> 00:07:09.820
I thought I saw a ship.

00:07:11.440 --> 00:07:12.390
Where?

00:07:14.620 --> 00:07:16.200
I'm sorry...

00:07:16.610 --> 00:07:18.340
I'm so sorry!

00:07:18.340 --> 00:07:21.130
I just... I thought I saw...

00:07:30.670 --> 00:07:33.220
It's all right, Shion-san.

00:07:33.220 --> 00:07:34.600
Everything is all right.

00:07:35.000 --> 00:07:39.080
Shion-san is delicate. This place
has gotta be too harsh for her.

00:07:39.770 --> 00:07:42.230
She's not like us rough types.

00:07:42.700 --> 00:07:43.500
Huh?

00:07:44.030 --> 00:07:45.410
That's weird...

00:07:45.410 --> 00:07:46.360
Huh?

00:07:47.260 --> 00:07:50.110
I wanna go home!

00:07:50.110 --> 00:07:51.360
H-Hey...

00:07:52.240 --> 00:07:54.630
Homare, you can cry, too!

00:07:54.630 --> 00:07:57.280
That's right, Homare-san!

00:07:57.660 --> 00:08:01.290
<i>I'm not good... with this kind of thing...</i>

00:08:02.120 --> 00:08:04.980
<i>This is the hardest thing I've had
to deal with since coming to this island.</i>

00:08:04.980 --> 00:08:05.860
<i>Papa...</i>

00:08:07.100 --> 00:08:10.200
When things are tough, when
you're sad, have a barbecue.

00:08:10.200 --> 00:08:12.710
You can overcome most
things in life with that.

00:08:12.710 --> 00:08:13.480
Okay!

00:08:22.260 --> 00:08:23.550
Hey, Shion.

00:08:25.090 --> 00:08:26.230
Come with me a sec.

00:08:28.980 --> 00:08:30.070
What is it?

00:08:32.390 --> 00:08:37.010
<i>Could it be... she's angry with me
for being so weepy this morning?</i>

00:08:42.020 --> 00:08:43.000
This is it.

00:08:43.640 --> 00:08:47.480
Usually, this place is
underwater, but it's low tide now.

00:08:47.480 --> 00:08:48.820
Dig up where you're standing.

00:08:48.820 --> 00:08:49.420
Huh?

00:08:51.300 --> 00:08:52.300
Here?

00:08:53.550 --> 00:08:54.910
<i>You regret what you did yet?</i>

00:08:54.910 --> 00:08:57.000
<i>My regret is deeper than the ocean...</i>

00:08:57.000 --> 00:08:57.840
No!

00:08:57.840 --> 00:08:59.320
I'm sorry! I was wrong—

00:08:59.320 --> 00:09:00.150
Shion.

00:09:00.630 --> 00:09:01.720
What are you doing?

00:09:02.120 --> 00:09:03.490
Hurry up.

00:09:03.910 --> 00:09:04.980
R-Right!

00:09:08.160 --> 00:09:10.620
Wh-Wha? A fish?

00:09:11.550 --> 00:09:12.940
Nice work, Shion.

00:09:13.710 --> 00:09:17.110
Before, when I was diving, 
I thought maybe...

00:09:17.810 --> 00:09:20.530
Wrasse really do sleep buried in the sand.

00:09:21.950 --> 00:09:23.750
Let's catch them together, Shion.

00:09:23.750 --> 00:09:24.960
All right!

00:09:30.920 --> 00:09:33.510
Right. That should do it.

00:09:33.510 --> 00:09:36.670
Th-That's amazing. We caught so many!

00:09:36.670 --> 00:09:37.450
Yeah.

00:09:37.450 --> 00:09:39.350
Thank you, Homare-san.

00:09:39.350 --> 00:09:41.850
I... I feel a lot better...

00:09:41.850 --> 00:09:44.020
With these, we can have a barbecue today.

00:09:44.020 --> 00:09:46.340
What? How perfectly lovely!

00:09:46.340 --> 00:09:48.900
You don't have to hug me
over every little thing.

00:09:51.250 --> 00:09:54.000
<i>It's just as you said, Papa.</i>

00:09:54.000 --> 00:09:55.820
<i>Grill 'em well!</i>

00:09:57.160 --> 00:09:59.230
We didn't find anything...

00:09:59.230 --> 00:10:00.830
No, we didn't...

00:10:01.370 --> 00:10:03.030
Where were you?

00:10:03.030 --> 00:10:03.660
Huh?

00:10:03.660 --> 00:10:05.660
Wow! Those are fish!

00:10:05.660 --> 00:10:07.290
Amazing! There are so many!

00:10:07.580 --> 00:10:09.240
It's a barbecue party!

00:10:10.690 --> 00:10:12.610
We should get ready, too!

00:10:12.610 --> 00:10:13.490
Yes!

00:10:15.820 --> 00:10:17.720
My, what a lovely fragrance!

00:10:17.720 --> 00:10:19.690
It's tea made from spicewood branches.

00:10:19.690 --> 00:10:21.910
I never thought I'd be able
to drink tea in this place.

00:10:21.910 --> 00:10:25.140
You can't have a party without
something delicious to drink.

00:10:25.420 --> 00:10:27.560
Shion-san, would you bring the cups?

00:10:28.120 --> 00:10:30.040
We don't have any cups.

00:10:30.600 --> 00:10:32.770
We do. They're over there.

00:10:35.260 --> 00:10:35.980
We can't!

00:10:35.980 --> 00:10:38.240
Shion-san, let's just compromise on this.

00:10:39.440 --> 00:10:40.410
Now...

00:10:40.870 --> 00:10:42.820
to our safety and health...

00:10:44.450 --> 00:10:46.770
Cheers!

00:10:49.000 --> 00:10:51.710
<b>Ahh...</b>

00:10:51.710 --> 00:10:53.580
It has such a nice aroma.

00:10:53.580 --> 00:10:55.880
It's like high grade oolong tea.

00:10:55.880 --> 00:10:58.360
Shall we move on to the main dish?

00:10:58.360 --> 00:10:59.050
Yes!

00:11:06.840 --> 00:11:08.940
Fish! Fish! Fish!

00:11:08.940 --> 00:11:11.130
Don't eat too quickly and choke.

00:11:12.760 --> 00:11:13.900
It's delicious!

00:11:26.910 --> 00:11:28.180
Everything's all right.

00:11:28.880 --> 00:11:31.930
Everyone! We're all going
to make it home together!

00:11:32.700 --> 00:11:34.280
Yeah!

00:11:44.850 --> 00:11:48.410
You know, when I was a kid,
I had a rabbit as a pet.

00:11:48.410 --> 00:11:51.180
So, to be honest, if we don't
catch one, I'm okay with that.

00:11:51.180 --> 00:11:55.810
Wasn't it you who said,
"Next time I'm gonna be heartless"?

00:11:56.200 --> 00:11:59.070
We won't survive with that
kind of half-hearted mindset.

00:11:59.070 --> 00:12:01.300
I know. I really do.

00:12:03.400 --> 00:12:04.390
Hey...

00:12:04.390 --> 00:12:05.700
Doesn't this mean...

00:12:06.350 --> 00:12:08.330
The trap was tripped.

00:12:08.330 --> 00:12:09.870
Seriously?

00:12:09.870 --> 00:12:12.190
Look. The end of the rope...

00:12:12.770 --> 00:12:15.210
If it's over there, that means...

00:12:16.500 --> 00:12:19.360
it's still alive, right?

00:12:25.720 --> 00:12:29.930
Next time, Case 6: "Rabbit Tasting."

00:12:28.010 --> 00:12:29.930
<b>Rabbit Tasting</b>
